# The circle tour: one full CCW circle, driven as eight arc twists.
#
# SIZING (2026-09-01). r = 300 mm. A circle driven CCW from a point on
# its own circumference puts its centre 90 deg to the left, so it spans
# +-r in x and 0..2r in y from the start: 600 x 600 mm. Against the
# working budget of +-550 x +-350 mm (tours/FIELD.md) that is the
# largest round radius that fits the tight axis. Stage the robot at
# (0, -300) relative to the field centre so the circle sits centred.
#
# The earlier 150 mm radius was sized against a smaller usable area and
# left half the field unused; before that, 250 mm was sized against the
# FULL field rather than the usable part and drove the robot to
# (182, 376) mm, after which the next tour failed against the north
# rail.
#
# ARC SEGMENTS ARE 45 DEG BY HISTORY. moveX() used to split any move
# with a nonzero distance and |rotation| >= 50 deg into a pivot THEN a
# straight, so the original single 360 deg arc drove the whole circle
# as one 942 mm STRAIGHT LINE (MEASURED gopiv 2026-09-01, closure
# 942.2 mm), and a 90 deg version drew a square. That split is gone
# (reports/move-x-arc-space-20260906.md, 2026-09-07): one 360 deg arc
# is now a circle. The 45 deg steps are kept, not required.
#
#   v = omega * r, with omega = 47.75 deg/s = 0.8333 rad/s
#   -> v = 0.8333 * 300 = 250 mm/s, matching the other tours' cruise.

# NO SET BLOCK (removed 2026-09-06, same reason as square.tour). This
# file used to carry `SET twist_hold_gain 8` -- a retune field_dance.py
# had already dropped as harmful on this engine, and the one line of
# the four that is still a LIVE ordinal (config_fields.h ordinal 7) --
# plus `SET speed_floor / yaw_taper / pivot_overrun`, all RETIRED or
# renamed since the config consolidation and answered with `err`. A
# tour is a benchmark of the firmware's defaults; it must not retune
# the robot. The pivot-tuning notes that justified the block are in
# diamond.tour and reports/gopiv-closure-20260901.md.

REPEAT 8

MARK circle
TWIST vx=250 omega=47.75 angle=45 timeout=6

END
STOP dwell=0.5
